# A text-changing effect is no copiable value (CR 707.2: the copiable values are what is printed, modified only by other
# copy effects, face-down status and "as ... enters" abilities; text-changing effects are not copied). Bot1's Mind Bend
# makes its Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth say "Each land is an Island". Bot2's Vesuva then enters as a copy of that Urborg: the
# copy says "Each land is a Swamp", as Urborg was printed. Both apply (each player controls one Urborg, so the legend rule
# leaves both, CR 704.5j): every land is an Island and a Swamp in addition to its other types - Bot1's Urborg and Bot2's
# copy among them - where a copied text change would have made them Islands alone.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth
Mind Bend
Island x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Vesuva
Forest x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate(Ability: {U})
Bot1.Hand.Mind Bend.Cast(Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Modes(Replace a basic land type)
Bot1.Modes(Swamp)
Bot1.Modes(Island)
? Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Subtypes = Forest; Island
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Vesuva.Play
Bot2.Accept
Bot2.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth)

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth.Subtypes = Island; Swamp
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Subtypes = Island; Swamp
Bot2.Battlefield.Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth.Subtypes = Island; Swamp
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Subtypes = Forest; Island; Swamp
